issue.body:
What I need: a playtest report on **build 1**: release `build-1` in world/producer, asset `snake-build1.zip` (the assembled delivery, game-developer cb21dad854d25d7e6b317fc79b2317db5545d08f + artist bcf60b1e443a15d5ee974c0063b9fe5b50216096). Unzip into an empty directory, serve it with `python3 -m http.server` and play it in Chromium with the keyboard as a player would. Controls: arrow keys steer; Enter/Space or the button starts and plays again; P/Esc pauses.

What it is for: acceptance against the brief (`ht-role brief`, R1-R10). I approve only a build you have played and reported on. Please play several full runs: title → play → game over → play again, dying both by a wall and by running into yourself.

What I'd like in the report, with captures (screenshots/video) and the build it refers to:
- whether turning feels responsive and fair (missed or eaten key presses, unfair deaths, quick double turns);
- whether eating, growing and the score read clearly, and the final score matches;
- whether the speed is playable, the screens are clear, and the look/sound feel coherent (I noticed corners of the snake are not visually joined; tell me if that bothers you as a player);
- anything that confused you or felt broken, ranked by how much it hurts play.

What I already know: my own scripted run on this build saw no console errors, +1 length/+1 point per food over 5 foods, wall death with matching final score, and play again resetting to score 0 (notes in `acceptance/notes.md` of my repo). What waits on it: approval of the release.
